WiFi FTP Server - GitHub APK build error fix
============================================

The build log reports 11 missing string resources in activity_main.xml.
Do NOT edit the 339-line activity_main.xml file.

STEP 1
Open this file in GitHub:
app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml

STEP 2
Click the pencil (Edit) icon.

STEP 3
Find the last line:
</resources>

Paste the following 11 lines IMMEDIATELY ABOVE </resources>:

    <string name="copy_address">Copy address</string>
    <string name="storage_permission_required">Storage permission is required to share files</string>
    <string name="grant_access">Grant access</string>
    <string name="port">Port</string>
    <string name="username">Username</string>
    <string name="password">Password</string>
    <string name="shared_folder">Shared folder</string>
    <string name="read_only">Read-only (no upload, delete or rename)</string>
    <string name="start_server">Start server</string>
    <string name="connect_from_windows">Connect from Windows</string>
    <string name="battery_optimization_settings">Battery optimization settings</string>

STEP 4
Click Commit changes and commit directly to the main branch.

STEP 5
Open Actions and check the new Build Android APK run.

NOTES
- This fixes the 11 missing resource names shown in the supplied build log.
- It does not guarantee the entire APK build succeeds; other issues may appear later.
- These added default English strings will be used where a Persian translation with the same name is missing.
- The existing strings.xml entries should be left untouched.
